<code>assert \result == null => this.isEmpty();</code>

However, based on the comment "@@@ If the deque is empty, then the result is null", the more accurate assertion should be:

<code>assert this.isEmpty() => \result == null;</code>

This ensures that if the deque is empty, the result of `pollFirst()` is indeed `null`.--------------------<code>assert this.isEmpty() => \result == null;</code>--------------------<code>assert this.isEmpty() => \result == null;</code>--------------------